# Maintainer Notes – pkg-tqftpserv

## Component

tqftpserv is a TFTP server that runs on top of the AF_QIPCRTR (QRTR) socket
type. It serves files from the Linux filesystem to remote processors
(modem, Wi-Fi, sensors, ...) on Qualcomm SoCs. This package is based on the
Ubuntu resolute source package `tqftpserv 1.1.1-1`.

## Upstream

- Repository: https://github.com/linux-msm/tqftpserv
- Branch: upstream/latest (tag `upstream/1.1.1`)
- Packaging branch: qcom/ubuntu/resolute (ubuntu)
- Upstream contact: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@linaro.org>

## Maintainer

Qualcomm Linux Team <linux-mainline@quicinc.com>

## Build

```bash
# Clone and switch to packaging branch
git clone https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/pkg-tqftpserv.git
cd pkg-tqftpserv
git checkout qcom/ubuntu/resolute

# Install build dependencies (libqrtr-dev, libzstd-dev, meson, systemd-dev, ...)
sudo apt-get build-dep .

# Build
gbp buildpackage --git-export-dir=../build-area
```

## Install and verify

```bash
sudo dpkg -i ../build-area/tqftpserv_1.1.1_arm64.deb
systemctl status tqftpserv.service
```

## Notes

- Packaging (control, rules, install files, udeb) is inherited from the Ubuntu
  resolute `tqftpserv 1.1.1-1` source package; changelog history is preserved.
- Changelog version is the bare upstream tag `1.1.1` per QLI Ubuntu convention.
  Note that dpkg orders `1.1.1` *below* the archive's `1.1.1-1`.
- Ubuntu branches do not use DEBUSINE CI; no debusine workflow stubs are added.
